---
// Honest limits · the things Rikiki deliberately doesn't do.
// Lists the rejected features so visitors can self-disqualify quickly.
---

<section id="limits" class="limits">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Honest limits</p>
    <h2>Not the right tool when…</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Rikiki is opinionated. Here is what we deliberately didn't build,
      so you can decide in 60 seconds whether it fits.
    </p>

    <ul class="grid">
      <li>
        <strong>You want a WYSIWYG editor.</strong>
        Rikiki is "write HTML, open in a browser". There is no builder UI
        and there won't be one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You need PowerPoint-style animations on shapes.</strong>
        Per-element timeline animations live in Keynote and Slidev, not here.
        We do slide-level transitions (fade / slide / zoom / flip) and that's it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You want a hosted SaaS.</strong>
        There is none. You host the static files yourself · S3, GitHub Pages,
        an nginx alias, whatever.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You need PowerPoint export.</strong>
        Rikiki produces HTML. <code>.pptx</code> output is not on the roadmap.
        You can browser-print to PDF (we recommend Chromium with print backgrounds on).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You're allergic to Web Components.</strong>
        The framework is Custom Elements + Shadow DOM at its core. If your
        team policy bans them, this isn't your tool.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .limits {
    background: var(--rik-surface-page);
    padding: var(--rik-space-7) var(--rik-space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .inner { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rik-text-default);
    color: var(--rik-surface-page);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--rik-radius-pill);
    font: 700 var(--rik-font-size-xs)/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-mega);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-lead);
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-6);
  }
  .grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--rik-space-3) var(--rik-space-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .grid li {
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    padding: var(--rik-space-3) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .grid li strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .grid li code {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: rgba(42, 37, 32, 0.06);
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
</style>
